{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is linked to Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through a chain of targets involving 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline. This quinoline compound acts as a target of benzocaine, which in turn influences the activity of the receptor subunit. The evidence suggests that benzocaine may modulate the function of this receptor through a mechanism involving the quinoline compound, which is a known target of benzocaine. The presence of multiple pathways connecting benzocaine to the receptor subunit gamma-2 indicates a potential role for the quinoline compound in mediating the interaction between benzocaine and the receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where benzocaine exerts its effects via a shared target, 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which in turn influences the receptor subunit gamma-2. This suggests a complex, multi-step interaction that may involve the quinoline compound as a critical mediator.",
